.TH SWEETIDLE 1 "November 9, 2026" "sweetidle 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sweetidle \- Wayland idle management daemon for the Sweets compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sweetidle
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B sweetidle status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B sweetidle pause
.br
.B sweetidle resume
.br
.B sweetidle reload
.br
.B sweetidle
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.B \-\-check-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sweetidle
is a lightweight Wayland idle daemon for the Sweets compositor.
It uses
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
to run commands when you go idle and when you return.
It also runs sleep, resume, lock, and unlock hooks, and respects idle
inhibitors.
Lock and unlock hooks need Linux logind.
Sleep hooks need logind on Linux or the rc hook on FreeBSD.
.PP
With no command, it runs in the foreground until stopped.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show daemon, listener, idle-hint, and inhibitor state.
.TP
.B "status --json"
Print the same state as one JSON object.
.TP
.B pause
Stop idle timers and clear the idle hint.
Running commands and sleep and lock hooks still run.
.TP
.B resume
Restart idle timers from zero.
.TP
.B reload
Queue a config reload. Check the logs for the result.
An invalid config keeps the old one active.
Changing a listener that already timed out rejects the reload.
Retry once you are active again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-c " PATH ", \-\-config " PATH
Use the config at
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the config and exit.
Also rejects features this platform does not support.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-json
JSON output for
.BR status .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config is
.IR ~/.config/sweetidle/config.toml :
UTF-8 TOML, at most 1 MiB.
Unknown fields are errors.
Timeouts are seconds from 1 to 4294967.
Commands must not be empty and run through
.BR "sh -c" .
stdin and stdout are
.IR /dev/null ;
stderr is inherited from sweetidle.
.PP
Optional
.B [general]
fields:
.TP
.B lock_command
Run on a logind lock request.
.TP
.B unlock_command
Run on a logind unlock request.
Only set this if your locker has a safe unlock command.
.TP
.B before_sleep_command
Run before suspend.
.TP
.B after_resume_command
Run after resume.
.TP
.B wait_before_sleep
Hold suspend until the before-sleep command exits: up to logind's max delay
on Linux, 4 seconds on FreeBSD.
Use a locker that returns only once locked.
Defaults to true.
.TP
.B ignore_dbus_inhibit
Ignore
.B org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
inhibitors.
Defaults to false.
.TP
.B ignore_systemd_inhibit
Ignore systemd-logind idle inhibitors.
Defaults to false.
No effect on FreeBSD.
.PP
Optional
.B [idle_hint]
has one required
.BR timeout .
After that many idle seconds, logind is told the session is idle.
Linux only.
.PP
Each
.B [[listener]]
accepts:
.TP
.B timeout
Idle seconds. Required.
.TP
.B on_timeout
Run when the timeout expires.
.TP
.B on_resume
Run when activity returns, only if
.B on_timeout
ran.
.TP
.B ignore_inhibit
Run despite all idle inhibitors.
Requires
.B ext_idle_notifier_v1
version 2.
Defaults to false.
.SH EXAMPLE CONFIGURATION
A Linux example.
On FreeBSD, drop
.B lock_command
and
.BR [idle_hint] .
.EX
[general]
lock_command = "veila lock --wait-ready"
before_sleep_command = "veila lock --wait-ready"
wait_before_sleep = true

[idle_hint]
timeout = 300

[[listener]]
timeout = 300
on_timeout = "veila lock --wait-ready"
ignore_inhibit = true

[[listener]]
timeout = 600
on_timeout = "sweets msg output-power '*' off"
on_resume = "sweets msg output-power '*' on"
.EE
.SH INHIBITORS
Listeners respect compositor, ScreenSaver D-Bus, and systemd-logind
.B idle
inhibitors by default.
The ScreenSaver service answers at
.I /org/freedesktop/ScreenSaver
and
.IR /ScreenSaver .
If another service owns that name, as niri does, sweetidle leaves D-Bus
inhibitors to it.
.PP
.B status
lists D-Bus and systemd inhibitors.
Compositor inhibitors are not visible to clients.
systemd monitoring shows as enabled, ignored, or unsupported
.RB ( inhibitors.systemd_status
in JSON).
.SH CONTROL SOCKET
Commands use
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetidle.sock
(mode 0600).
While it is live, a second daemon will not start.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop the daemon.
Running commands keep running.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Same as
.BR reload .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Base of the default config path.
Must be absolute unless
.B \-\-config
is set.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the control socket. Required.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display to connect to.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
Logind session to use.
If unset, logind picks the caller's session, or the graphical session for a
systemd user service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sweetidle/config.toml
Default user configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetidle.sock
Local control socket.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/sweetidle.service
Systemd user service.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/sweetidle.1
This manual page.
.SH SYSTEMD USER SERVICE
.B sweetidle.service
runs with
.BR graphical-session.target :
.PP
.EX
systemctl --user enable --now sweetidle.service
.EE
.PP
Don't also start sweetidle from your compositor config.
.SH FREEBSD
Tested on FreeBSD 15.1 amd64 with Sweets.
Build with Cargo and start sweetidle from the compositor's startup config.
It needs the session's
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
and
.BR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS .
Without a session bus, set
.BR ignore_dbus_inhibit .
The example config is
.IR config/freebsd.toml .
.PP
Logs go to stderr.
Redirect them or use the compositor's session log.
.PP
Sleep hooks need the rc hook:
.PP
.EX
sudo install -m 755 target/release/sweetidle /usr/local/bin/sweetidle
sudo install -m 755 freebsd/sweetidle_sleep /usr/local/etc/rc.d/sweetidle_sleep
sudo sysrc sweetidle_sleep_enable=YES
sudo sysrc sweetidle_sleep_runtime_dirs="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"
.EE
.PP
Then set
.B before_sleep_command
and
.B after_resume_command
and restart sweetidle.
Commands run as your user; the root hook only sends notifications.
.sp
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 2
With
.BR wait_before_sleep ,
the command must succeed within 4 seconds or suspend is cancelled.
Without it, the hook does not wait for locking.
.IP \(bu 2
After-resume runs once, on resume or on cancel.
.IP \(bu 2
A new suspend fails while an older before-sleep command still runs.
.IP \(bu 2
FreeBSD's 10-second forced-suspend fallback still applies.
The hook is not a system-wide inhibitor.
.IP \(bu 2
For multiple sessions, list up to 16 absolute runtime dirs, space separated,
without whitespace in the paths.
.IP \(bu 2
Set
.B sweetidle_sleep_command
in rc.conf if the binary is elsewhere.
.IP \(bu 2
Set
.B sweetidle_sleep_enable=NO
to turn the hook off.
.IP \(bu 2
Adding the first sleep hook or removing the last needs a restart.
.PD
.PP
The hook uses the rc-only commands
.BR "before-sleep ID" ,
.BR "after-resume ID" ,
and
.B "cancel-sleep ID"
on a separate
.I sweetidle-sleep.sock
(mode 0600).
.PP
.BR lock_command ,
.BR unlock_command ,
and
.B [idle_hint]
need logind and are rejected.
systemd inhibitors are unsupported.
ConsoleKit is not supported.
Use a listener to lock on idle.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sweetidle
returns 0 on success and 2 on any error, including
.IR "compositor closed the Wayland connection" .
A service manager can then restart it after a compositor crash.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a config file:
.PP
.EX
sweetidle --config ./config.toml --check-config
.EE
.PP
Run with debug logs:
.PP
.EX
sweetidle --verbose --config ./config.toml
.EE
.PP
Read the paused state:
.PP
.EX
sweetidle status --json | jq -r .paused
.EE
.PP
Reload the config:
.PP
.EX
pkill -HUP -x sweetidle
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR loginctl (1)
.PP
